"A beautiful begining yet the future's unknowing,\nCame to the first room, though then I knew no meaning.\n\nDay by day, I met new people,\nEveryday I, learned somethin' new,\nWhen to help and when to ask,\nEverytime, it was a novel hue.\n\nLearned to sit, and to talk,\nLearned to behave, and to walk,\nHow to take and when to mock,\nWhen to care and where to stop.\n\nInfluences were new,\nSo were the experiences, yes\nUnderstanding was still due,\nSo were the friendly fuss.\n\nMany came, and many left,\nAttachment was to stay naturally,\nUes we did learn, but forgot everytime,\nAttachment was to fade gradually.\n\nFrom room to room,\nThen to a new building,\nYes the mistakes happened,\nSometimes against the upbringing.\n\nWe learned to have fun,\nThough many did not,\nSome got a bad experience,\nFew just gave themselves a shot.\n\nUnderstood many things,\nYes, beyond academics,\nDid learn what not to do,\nBut still forgot many dynamics.\n\nBuildings changed,\nMet new people,\nThe previous left,\nBut stayed in the heart.\n\nComs didn't end,\nBond didn't change,\nThe true ones never faded,\nAnd the new ones got a new start.\n\nMade new friends,\nMade alleged families,\nUnderstood the crooked ones,\nAnd the prerenders and the anomalies.\n\nThe journey won't end,\nFor the companions are still alive,\nThe one we called a friend,\nWe'll together improve and thrive"